<!-- SDA -->
<section class="sda" id="sda">
  <div class="sdagrid">
    <div>
      <div class="tag">What is SDA?</div>
      <h2 class="sh">Housing that's<br><em>funded for you.</em></h2>
      <p style="font-size:16px;font-weight:300;color:var(--ink-mid);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:16px;">Specialist Disability Accommodation (SDA) is housing funded through Australia's NDIS for people with extreme functional impairment or very high support needs.</p>
      <p style="font-size:16px;font-weight:300;color:var(--ink-mid);line-height:1.85;margin-bottom:36px;">That means your rent is covered through your NDIS plan — so you can focus on living well, not on housing costs.</p>
      <a href="https://www.ndis.gov.au" target="_blank" class="wlink">Learn more at NDIS.gov.au <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M5 12h14M12 5l7 7-7 7"/></svg></a>
    </div>
    <div class="sdabubbles">
      <div class="bubble">
        <h4>How does SDA funding work?</h4>
        <p>SDA funding is paid directly to the landlord through your NDIS plan. Eligible participants can live in purpose-built accessible housing without paying standard rental costs out of pocket.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bubble">
        <h4>Am I eligible?</h4>
        <p>SDA is for NDIS participants with extreme functional impairment or very high support needs. Your support coordinator or NDIS planner can assess your eligibility and help you apply.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bubble">
        <h4>How do I apply?</h4>
        <p>Contact ADAPT Housing (SDA provider) about availability, or Challenge Community Services (SIL provider) about care and support arrangements. Reach out to us at Brookline and we'll connect you with the right people.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

